  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "train-departs",
      "pattern": "الـ[Noun] + يَنْطَلِقُ",
      "exampleArabic": "القطار ينطلق",
      "exampleTransliteration": "al-qiṭāru yanṭaliqu",
      "exampleEnglish": "The train departs.",
      "grammarNote": "اِنْطَلَقَ ('to depart/set off') is Form VII (اِنْفَعَلَ) — marked by an اِنْـ prefix. Like Forms V, VI, and VIII, its present-tense prefix takes fatha: أَنْطَلِقُ, تَنْطَلِقُ, تَنْطَلِقِينَ, يَنْطَلِقُ, نَنْطَلِقُ. Form VII often carries a sense of something happening 'by itself' rather than being done to something — القطار ينطلق ('the train departs') describes the train's own motion, not someone departing it. With this form, nine of the ten verb forms are now covered outside the base Form I; only Form IX (اِفْعَلَّ, used almost exclusively for colors and physical traits — e.g. اِحْمَرَّ 'to blush') is left out, deliberately, as too narrow to be worth its own level.",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_alqitaar_yantaliqu", "text": "القطار ينطلق" },
      "introducedInLevel": 73
    }
  ],
